@startuml build-expense-agent
title Building "expense-summarizer" — an agent is a FOLDER of data, consumed by steps that already exist
' Color code (same as before): application=green  domain=yellow  infrastructure=red
' NEW ring: YOUR AGENT FOLDER = orange. Arrows leaving a ring carry its color.
' Orange arrows answer: "which pipeline step eats this file?"

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

' ===================== YOUR AGENT (orange) — pure data, zero Python =====================
package "agents/expense-summarizer/   (what YOU write)" #FFF3E0 {
  class "agent.toml" as Toml <<config>> {
    name = "Expense Summarizer"
    tools_allow = [read, exec, write, find]
    model = "gemini/..."  (optional)
  }
  class "IDENTITY.md" as Identity <<prose>> {
    "You are the Expense Summarizer...
    reads expense files, totals the month,
    categorizes, produces a chart"
  }
  class "AGENTS.md" as Rules <<prose>> {
    file locations, CSV formats,
    categories, report layout,
    "never fabricate a transaction"
  }
  class "skills/monthly-report/SKILL.md" as Skill <<playbook>> {
    1. find this month's files
    2. parse  3. aggregate
    4. chart (matplotlib)  5. report
  }
  class "workspace/" as Workspace <<folder>> {
    your expense CSVs live here;
    tools run with this as cwd
  }
}

note bottom of Toml #FFF8DC
  NOT injected. NOT code. NO interface.
  The contract is FILE NAMES in a folder.
  Injection is for platform organs (engine,
  stores) — an agent is CONTENT, discovered
  at boot / registry.refresh().
end note

' ===================== domain (yellow) =====================
package "domain" #FEF7E0 {
  class AgentSpec {
    id = "expense-summarizer"
    instructions  <- IDENTITY+AGENTS text
    tools_allow / model / workspace
  }
}

' ===================== infrastructure (red) =====================
package "infrastructure" #FCE8E6 {
  class FileAgentRegistry {
    scans agents/<id>/ at boot/refresh
  }
  class SkillLoader {
    scans skills/ folders -> index
  }
  class "read / exec / write tools" as Tools {
    exec runs python: parse CSVs,
    matplotlib -> chart.png (artifact)
  }
}

' ===================== application (green) — the 7 steps you know =====================
package "application — AgentService.handle_message" #E6F4EA {
  class "step 1  resolve agent" as S1
  class "step 2  pick toolset" as S2
  class "step 3  make session" as S3
  class "step 5  build prompt" as S5
  class "step 6  recall" as S6
  class "step 7  engine.run (the loop)" as S7
}

' ---------- discovery (red: the platform reads your folder) ----------
FileAgentRegistry -[#D93025]-> Toml : reads
FileAgentRegistry -[#D93025]-> Identity : reads
FileAgentRegistry -[#D93025]-> Rules : reads
FileAgentRegistry -[#D93025]-> AgentSpec : builds ONE spec\nfrom the folder
SkillLoader -[#D93025]-> Skill : indexes (one line)

' ---------- consumption (orange: which step eats which file) ----------
AgentSpec -[#E8710A]-> S1 : folder name = the id\nresolved per session key
Toml -[#E8710A]-> S2 : tools_allow filters\nthe shared catalog
Toml -[#E8710A]-> S7 : model override rides\ninto engine.run(model=...)
Identity -[#E8710A]-> S5 : prompt section 3\n(via AgentSpec.instructions)
Rules -[#E8710A]-> S5 : prompt section 3
Skill -[#E8710A]-> S5 : one-line INDEX in prompt
Skill -[#E8710A]-> S7 : full playbook read ON DEMAND\n(an ordinary `read` tool call)
Workspace -[#E8710A]-> S7 : cwd for read/exec/write\n(parse files, save chart.png)
Workspace -[#E8710A]-> S3 : sessions partition under\nthe agent's state dir

' ---------- the run itself ----------
S7 -[#1E8E3E]-> Tools : the model calls them\nagainst YOUR files

note right of S7 #F0FFF0
  A turn: "summarize my June spending"
  model reads SKILL.md -> finds CSVs (find/read)
  -> exec python: totals + categories
  -> exec matplotlib -> chart.png artifact
  -> writes the report. Same spine as "hi" —
  only the CONTENT differs.
end note

note bottom of S5 #F0FFF0
  GOING LIVE: restart daemon (or any
  registry.refresh trigger) -> chat at
  session key agent:expense-summarizer:...
  Zero changes to container.py, zero
  new interfaces — the platform already
  had every step; you only fed it files.
end note

@enduml
